From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 21:50:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 098/117] drm/msm/shrinker: wait for active BOs only from
 kswapd

can_block() lets any direct reclaim wait for active BOs to become idle,
up to 10 jiffies per BO. Direct reclaim runs in the allocating task, and
for a GPU driver that is often a task the desktop depends on: the
compositor, or a task in the submit ioctl that holds the reservation
locks of its BOs while it pins them or allocates its submit tables.
Waiting there for the GPU turns memory pressure into a stall of that
task, and of everything waiting for its locks, for the length of the
scan; with mostly busy BOs the scan runs into the timeout BO after BO.

i915 reaps active objects only from kswapd, and the TTM shrink helpers
(ttm_bo_shrink_avoid_wait()) let only kswapd wait for the GPU. Do the
same: run the blocking active purge / evict stages from kswapd only.
Direct reclaim still purges and evicts idle BOs, and eviction_can_block
still turns blocking off entirely.

Problem and approach by yzddmr6 (linux-sm8750 tree da4b783e34bd,
"drm/msm/shrinker: Only block for active BOs from kswapd", no
Signed-off-by); re-implemented.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem_shrinker.c | 13 ++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem_shrinker.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem_shrinker.c
index 52a8f5faeb873..de0206988d4ee 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem_shrinker.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem_shrinker.c
@@ -28,12 +28,19 @@ static bool can_swap(void)
 	return enable_eviction && get_nr_swap_pages() > 0;
 }
 
+/*
+ * Wait for the GPU to idle a BO only from kswapd, as i915 and the TTM shrink
+ * helpers do. Direct reclaim runs in the allocating task, which may be the
+ * compositor or a task in the submit ioctl that holds the reservation locks of
+ * its BOs; blocking it on the GPU stalls it, and everyone waiting for those
+ * locks, for the whole scan. Direct reclaim still purges and evicts idle BOs.
+ */
 static bool can_block(struct shrink_control *sc)
 {
-	if (!eviction_can_block)
+	if (!eviction_can_block || !current_is_kswapd())
 		return false;
-	return (sc->gfp_mask & __GFP_DIRECT_RECLAIM) ||
-	       (current_is_kswapd() && (sc->gfp_mask & __GFP_KSWAPD_RECLAIM));
+
+	return sc->gfp_mask & __GFP_KSWAPD_RECLAIM;
 }
 
 static unsigned long
